And Abram gave him one-tenth of everything.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 14, 21, 'Then the king of Sodom said to Abram, "Give me the persons, but take the goods for yourself."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 14, 22, 'But Abram said to the king of Sodom, "I have sworn to the LORD, God Most High, maker of heaven and earth,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 14, 23, 'that I would not take a thread or a sandal-thong or anything that is yours, so that you might not say, "I have made Abram rich."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 14, 24, 'I will take nothing but what the young men have eaten, and the share of the men who went with me--Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre. Let them take their share."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


"Now you have conceived and shall bear a son;  
    you shall call him Ishmael,  
    for the LORD has given heed to your affliction.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 16, 12, 'He shall be a wild ass of a man,  
with his hand against everyone,  
    and everyone"s hand against him;  
and he shall live at odds with all his kin."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 16, 13, 'So she named the LORD who spoke to her, "You are El-roi"; for she said, "Have I really seen God and remained alive after seeing him?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 16, 14, 'Therefore the well was called Beer-lahai-roi; it lies between Kadesh and Bered.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 16, 15, 'Hagar bore Abram a son; and Abram named his son, whom Hagar bore, Ishmael.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 16, 16, 'Abram was eighty-six years old when Hagar bore him Ishmael.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);








"May you, our sister, become  
    thousands of myriads;  
may your offspring gain possession  
    of the gates of their foes."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 24, 61, 'Then Rebekah and her maids rose up, mounted the camels, and followed the man; thus the servant took Rebekah, and went his way.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 24, 62, 'Now Isaac had come from Beer-lahai-roi, and was settled in the Negeb.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 24, 63, 'Isaac went out in the evening to walk in the field; and looking up, he saw camels coming.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 24, 64, 'And Rebekah looked up, and when she saw Isaac, she slipped quickly from the camel,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 24, 65, 'and said to the servant, "Who is the man over there, walking in the field to meet us?" The servant said, "It is my master." So she took her veil and covered herself.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 24, 66, 'And the servant told Isaac all the things that he had done.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 24, 67, 'Then Isaac brought her into his mother Sarah"s tent. He took Rebekah, and she became his wife; and he loved her. So Isaac was comforted after his mother"s death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"Two nations are in your womb,  
    and two peoples born of you shall be divided;  
the one shall be stronger than the other,  
    the elder shall serve the younger."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 24, 'When her time to give birth was at hand, there were twins in her womb.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 25, 'The first came out red, all his body like a hairy mantle; so they named him Esau.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 26, 'Afterward his brother came out, with his hand gripping Esau"s heel; so he was named Jacob. Isaac was sixty years old when she bore them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 27, 'When the boys grew up, Esau was a skillful hunter, a man of the field, while Jacob was a quiet man, living in tents.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 28, 'Isaac loved Esau, because he was fond of game; but Rebekah loved Jacob.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 29, 'Once when Jacob was cooking a stew, Esau came in from the field, and he was famished.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Esau Sells His Birthright'),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 30, 'Esau said to Jacob, "Let me eat some of that red stuff, for I am famished!" (Therefore he was called Edom.)', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 31, 'Jacob said, "First sell me your birthright."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 32, 'Esau said, "I am about to die; of what use is a birthright to me?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 33, 'Jacob said, "Swear to me first." So he swore to him, and sold his birthright to Jacob.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 25, 34, 'Then Jacob gave Esau bread and lentil stew, and he ate and drank, and rose and went his way. Thus Esau despised his birthright.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


"Ah, the smell of my son  
    is like the smell of a field that the LORD has blessed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 28, 'May God give you of the dew of heaven,  
    and of the fatness of the earth,  
    and plenty of grain and wine.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 29, 'Let peoples serve you,  
    and nations bow down to you.  
Be lord over your brothers,  
    and may your mother"s sons bow down to you.  
Cursed be everyone who curses you,  
    and blessed be everyone who blesses you!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 30, 'As soon as Isaac had finished blessing Jacob, when Jacob had scarcely gone out from the presence of his father Isaac, his brother Esau came in from his hunting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Esau"s Lost Blessing'),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 31, 'He also prepared savory food, and brought it to his father. And he said to his father, "Let my father sit up and eat of his son"s game, so that you may bless me."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 32, 'His father Isaac said to him, "Who are you?" He answered, "I am your firstborn son, Esau."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 33, 'Then Isaac trembled violently, and said, "Who was it then that hunted game and brought it to me, and I ate it all before you came, and I have blessed him?--yes, and blessed he shall be!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 34, 'When Esau heard his father"s words, he cried out with an exceedingly great and bitter cry, and said to his father, "Bless me, me also, father!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 35, 'But he said, "Your brother came deceitfully, and he has taken away your blessing."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 36, 'Esau said, "Is he not rightly named Jacob? For he has supplanted me these two times. He took away my birthright; and look, now he has taken away my blessing." Then he said, "Have you not reserved a blessing for me?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 37, 'Isaac answered Esau, "I have already made him your lord, and I have given him all his brothers as servants, and with grain and wine I have sustained him. What then can I do for you, my son?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 38, 'Esau said to his father, "Have you only one blessing, father? Bless me, me also, father!" And Esau lifted up his voice and wept.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 39, 'Then his father Isaac answered him:
"See, away from the fatness of the earth shall your home be,  
    and away from the dew of heaven on high.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 40, 'By your sword you shall live,  
    and you shall serve your brother;  
but when you break loose,  
    you shall break his yoke from your neck."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 41, 'Now Esau hated Jacob because of the blessing with which his father had blessed him, and Esau said to himself, "The days of mourning for my father are approaching; then I will kill my brother Jacob."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Jacob Escapes Esau"s Fury'),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 42, 'But the words of her elder son Esau were told to Rebekah; so she sent and called her younger son Jacob and said to him, "Your brother Esau is consoling himself by planning to kill you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 43, 'Now therefore, my son, obey my voice; flee at once to my brother Laban in Haran,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 44, 'and stay with him a while, until your brother"s fury turns away--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 45, 'until your brother"s anger against you turns away, and he forgets what you have done to him; then I will send, and bring you back from there. Why should I lose both of you in one day?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 27, 46, 'Then Rebekah said to Isaac, "I am weary of my life because of the Hittite women. If Jacob marries one of the Hittite women such as these, one of the women of the land, what good will my life be to me?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);








Now the sons of Jacob were twelve.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 35, 23, 'The sons of Leah: Reuben (Jacob"s firstborn), Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, and Zebulun.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 35, 24, 'The sons of Rachel: Joseph and Benjamin.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 35, 25, 'The sons of Bilhah, Rachel"s maid: Dan and Naphtali.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 35, 26, 'The sons of Zilpah, Leah"s maid: Gad and Asher. These were the sons of Jacob who were born to him in Paddan-aram.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 35, 27, 'Jacob came to his father Isaac at Mamre, or Kiriath-arba (that is, Hebron), where Abraham and Isaac had resided as aliens.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Death of Isaac'),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 35, 28, 'Now the days of Isaac were one hundred eighty years.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 35, 29, 'And Isaac breathed his last; he died and was gathered to his people, old and full of days; and his sons Esau and Jacob buried him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


Joseph, being seventeen years old, was shepherding the flock with his brothers; he was a helper to the sons of Bilhah and Zilpah, his father"s wives; and Joseph brought a bad report of them to their father.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 3, 'Now Israel loved Joseph more than any other of his children, because he was the son of his old age; and he had made him a long robe with sleeves.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 4, 'But when his brothers saw that their father loved him more than all his brothers, they hated him, and could not speak peaceably to him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 5, 'Once Joseph had a dream, and when he told it to his brothers, they hated him even more.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 6, 'He said to them, "Listen to this dream that I dreamed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 7, 'There we were, binding sheaves in the field. Suddenly my sheaf rose and stood upright; then your sheaves gathered around it, and bowed down to my sheaf."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 8, 'His brothers said to him, "Are you indeed to reign over us? Are you indeed to have dominion over us?" So they hated him even more because of his dreams and his words.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 9, 'He had another dream, and told it to his brothers, saying, "Look, I have had another dream: the sun, the moon, and eleven stars were bowing down to me."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 10, 'But when he told it to his father and to his brothers, his father rebuked him, and said to him, "What kind of dream is this that you have had? Shall we indeed come, I and your mother and your brothers, and bow to the ground before you?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 11, 'So his brothers were jealous of him, but his father kept the matter in mind.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 12, 'Now his brothers went to pasture their father"s flock near Shechem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Joseph Is Sold by His Brothers'),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 13, 'And Israel said to Joseph, "Are not your brothers pasturing the flock at Shechem? Come, I will send you to them." He answered, "Here I am."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 14, 'So he said to him, "Go now, see if it is well with your brothers and with the flock; and bring word back to me." So he sent him from the valley of Hebron.
He came to Shechem,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 15, 'and a man found him wandering in the fields; the man asked him, "What are you seeking?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 16, '"I am seeking my brothers," he said; "tell me, please, where they are pasturing the flock."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 17, 'The man said, "They have gone away, for I heard them say, "Let us go to Dothan."" So Joseph went after his brothers, and found them at Dothan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 18, 'They saw him from a distance, and before he came near to them, they conspired to kill him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 19, 'They said to one another, "Here comes this dreamer.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 20, 'Come now, let us kill him and throw him into one of the pits; then we shall say that a wild animal has devoured him, and we shall see what will become of his dreams."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 21, 'But when Reuben heard it, he delivered him out of their hands, saying, "Let us not take his life."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 22, 'Reuben said to them, "Shed no blood; throw him into this pit here in the wilderness, but lay no hand on him"--that he might rescue him out of their hand and restore him to his father.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 23, 'So when Joseph came to his brothers, they stripped him of his robe, the long robe with sleeves that he wore;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 24, 'and they took him and threw him into a pit. The pit was empty; there was no water in it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 25, 'Then they sat down to eat; and looking up they saw a caravan of Ishmaelites coming from Gilead, with their camels carrying gum, balm, and resin, on their way to carry it down to Egypt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 26, 'Then Judah said to his brothers, "What profit is it if we kill our brother and conceal his blood?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 27, 'Come, let us sell him to the Ishmaelites, and not lay our hands on him, for he is our brother, our own flesh." And his brothers agreed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 28, 'When some Midianite traders passed by, they drew Joseph up, lifting him out of the pit, and sold him to the Ishmaelites for twenty pieces of silver. And they took Joseph to Egypt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 29, 'When Reuben returned to the pit and saw that Joseph was not in the pit, he tore his clothes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 30, 'He returned to his brothers, and said, "The boy is gone; and I, where can I turn?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 31, 'Then they took Joseph"s robe, slaughtered a goat, and dipped the robe in the blood.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 32, 'They had the long robe with sleeves taken to their father, and they said, "This we have found; see now whether it is your son"s robe or not."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 33, 'He recognized it, and said, "It is my son"s robe! A wild animal has devoured him; Joseph is without doubt torn to pieces."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 34, 'Then Jacob tore his garments, and put sackcloth on his loins, and mourned for his son many days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 35, 'All his sons and all his daughters sought to comfort him; but he refused to be comforted, and said, "No, I shall go down to Sheol to my son, mourning." Thus his father bewailed him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 37, 36, 'Meanwhile the Midianites had sold him in Egypt to Potiphar, one of Pharaoh"s officials, the captain of the guard.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


Now Joseph was handsome and good-looking.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 7, 'And after a time his master"s wife cast her eyes on Joseph and said, "Lie with me."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 8, 'But he refused and said to his master"s wife, "Look, with me here, my master has no concern about anything in the house, and he has put everything that he has in my hand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 9, 'He is not greater in this house than I am, nor has he kept back anything from me except yourself, because you are his wife. How then could I do this great wickedness, and sin against God?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 10, 'And although she spoke to Joseph day after day, he would not consent to lie beside her or to be with her.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 11, 'One day, however, when he went into the house to do his work, and while no one else was in the house,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 12, 'she caught hold of his garment, saying, "Lie with me!" But he left his garment in her hand, and fled and ran outside.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 13, 'When she saw that he had left his garment in her hand and had fled outside,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 14, 'she called out to the members of her household and said to them, "See, my husband has brought among us a Hebrew to insult us! He came in to me to lie with me, and I cried out with a loud voice;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 15, 'and when he heard me raise my voice and cry out, he left his garment beside me, and fled outside."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 16, 'Then she kept his garment by her until his master came home,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 17, 'and she told him the same story, saying, "The Hebrew servant, whom you have brought among us, came in to me to insult me;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 18, 'but as soon as I raised my voice and cried out, he left his garment beside me, and fled outside."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 19, 'When his master heard the words that his wife spoke to him, saying, "This is the way your servant treated me," he became enraged.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 20, 'And Joseph"s master took him and put him into the prison, the place where the king"s prisoners were confined; he remained there in prison.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 21, 'But the LORD was with Joseph and showed him steadfast love; he gave him favor in the sight of the chief jailer.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 22, 'The chief jailer committed to Joseph"s care all the prisoners who were in the prison, and whatever was done there, he was the one who did it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 39, 23, 'The chief jailer paid no heed to anything that was in Joseph"s care, because the LORD was with him; and whatever he did, the LORD made it prosper.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);









"The God before whom my ancestors Abraham and Isaac walked,  
the God who has been my shepherd all my life to this day,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 48, 16, 'the angel who has redeemed me from all harm, bless the boys;  
and in them let my name be perpetuated, and the name of my ancestors Abraham and Isaac;  
and let them grow into a multitude on the earth."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 48, 17, 'When Joseph saw that his father laid his right hand on the head of Ephraim, it displeased him; so he took his father"s hand, to remove it from Ephraim"s head to Manasseh"s head.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 48, 18, 'Joseph said to his father, "Not so, my father! Since this one is the firstborn, put your right hand on his head."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 48, 19, 'But his father refused, and said, "I know, my son, I know; he also shall become a people, and he also shall be great. Nevertheless his younger brother shall be greater than he, and his offspring shall become a multitude of nations."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 48, 20, 'So he blessed them that day, saying,
"By you Israel will invoke blessings, saying,  
"God make you like Ephraim and like Manasseh.""
So he put Ephraim ahead of Manasseh.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 48, 21, 'Then Israel said to Joseph, "I am about to die, but God will be with you and will bring you again to the land of your ancestors.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 48, 22, 'I now give to you one portion more than to your brothers, the portion that I took from the hand of the Amorites with my sword and with my bow."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

    listen to Israel your father.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 3, 'Reuben, you are my firstborn,  
    my might and the first fruits of my vigor,  
    excelling in rank and excelling in power.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 4, 'Unstable as water, you shall no longer excel  
    because you went up onto your father"s bed;  
    then you defiled it--you went up onto my couch!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 5, 'Simeon and Levi are brothers;  
    weapons of violence are their swords.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 6, 'May I never come into their council;  
    may I not be joined to their company--  
for in their anger they killed men,  
    and at their whim they hamstrung oxen.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 7, 'Cursed be their anger, for it is fierce,  
    and their wrath, for it is cruel!  
I will divide them in Jacob,  
    and scatter them in Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 8, 'Judah, your brothers shall praise you;  
    your hand shall be on the neck of your enemies;  
    your father"s sons shall bow down before you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 9, 'Judah is a lion"s whelp;  
    from the prey, my son, you have gone up.  
He crouches down, he stretches out like a lion,  
    like a lioness--who dares rouse him up?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 10, 'The scepter shall not depart from Judah,  
    nor the ruler"s staff from between his feet,  
until tribute comes to him;  
    and the obedience of the peoples is his.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 11, 'Binding his foal to the vine  
    and his donkey"s colt to the choice vine,  
he washes his garments in wine  
    and his robe in the blood of grapes;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 12, 'his eyes are darker than wine,  
    and his teeth whiter than milk.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 13, 'Zebulun shall settle at the shore of the sea;  
    he shall be a haven for ships,  
    and his border shall be at Sidon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 14, 'Issachar is a strong donkey,  
    lying down between the sheepfolds;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 15, 'he saw that a resting place was good,  
    and that the land was pleasant;  
so he bowed his shoulder to the burden,  
    and became a slave at forced labor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 16, 'Dan shall judge his people  
    as one of the tribes of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 17, 'Dan shall be a snake by the roadside,  
    a viper along the path,  
that bites the horse"s heels  
    so that its rider falls backward.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 18, 'I wait for your salvation, O LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 19, 'Gad shall be raided by raiders,  
    but he shall raid at their heels.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 20, 'Asher"s food shall be rich,  
    and he shall provide royal delicacies.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 21, 'Naphtali is a doe let loose  
    that bears lovely fawns.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 22, 'Joseph is a fruitful bough,  
    a fruitful bough by a spring;  
    his branches run over the wall.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 23, 'The archers fiercely attacked him;  
    they shot at him and pressed him hard.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 24, 'Yet his bow remained taut,  
    and his arms were made agile  
by the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob,  
    by the name of the Shepherd, the Rock of Israel,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 25, 'by the God of your father, who will help you,  
    by the Almighty who will bless you  
    with blessings of heaven above,  
blessings of the deep that lies beneath,  
    blessings of the breasts and of the womb.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 26, 'The blessings of your father  
    are stronger than the blessings of the eternal mountains,  
    the bounties of the everlasting hills;  
may they be on the head of Joseph,  
    on the brow of him who was set apart from his brothers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 27, 'Benjamin is a ravenous wolf,  
    in the morning devouring the prey,  
    and at evening dividing the spoil."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 28, 'All these are the twelve tribes of Israel, and this is what their father said to them when he blessed them, blessing each one of them with a suitable blessing.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 29, 'Then he charged them, saying to them, "I am about to be gathered to my people. Bury me with my ancestors--in the cave in the field of Ephron the Hittite,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Jacob"s Death and Burial'),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 30, 'in the cave in the field at Machpelah, near Mamre, in the land of Canaan, in the field that Abraham bought from Ephron the Hittite as a burial site.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 31, 'There Abraham and his wife Sarah were buried; there Isaac and his wife Rebekah were buried; and there I buried Leah--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 32, 'the field and the cave that is in it were purchased from the Hittites."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(1, 'Kej', 'Genesis', 49, 33, 'When Jacob ended his charge to his sons, he drew up his feet into the bed, breathed his last, and was gathered to his people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



But Moses fled from Pharaoh. He settled in the land of Midian, and sat down by a well.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 16, 'The priest of Midian had seven daughters. They came to draw water, and filled the troughs to water their father"s flock.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 17, 'But some shepherds came and drove them away. Moses got up and came to their defense and watered their flock.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 18, 'When they returned to their father Reuel, he said, "How is it that you have come back so soon today?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 19, 'They said, "An Egyptian helped us against the shepherds; he even drew water for us and watered the flock."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 20, 'He said to his daughters, "Where is he? Why did you leave the man? Invite him to break bread."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 21, 'Moses agreed to stay with the man, and he gave Moses his daughter Zipporah in marriage.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 22, 'She bore a son, and he named him Gershom; for he said, "I have been an alien residing in a foreign land."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 23, 'After a long time the king of Egypt died. The Israelites groaned under their slavery, and cried out. Out of the slavery their cry for help rose up to God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 24, 'God heard their groaning, and God remembered his covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 2, 25, 'God looked upon the Israelites, and God took notice of them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

This is my name forever,  
and this my title for all generations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 3, 16, 'Go and assemble the elders of Israel, and say to them, "The LORD, the God of your ancestors, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Jacob, has appeared to me, saying: I have given heed to you and to what has been done to you in Egypt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 3, 17, 'I declare that I will bring you up out of the misery of Egypt, to the land of the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites, a land flowing with milk and honey."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 3, 18, 'They will listen to your voice; and you and the elders of Israel shall go to the king of Egypt and say to him, "The LORD, the God of the Hebrews, has met with us; let us now go a three days" journey into the wilderness, so that we may sacrifice to the LORD our God."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 3, 19, 'I know, however, that the king of Egypt will not let you go unless compelled by a mighty hand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 3, 20, 'So I will stretch out my hand and strike Egypt with all my wonders that I will perform in it; after that he will let you go.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 3, 21, 'I will bring this people into such favor with the Egyptians that, when you go, you will not go empty-handed;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 3, 22, 'each woman shall ask her neighbor and any woman living in the neighbor"s house for jewelry of silver and of gold, and clothing, and you shall put them on your sons and on your daughters; and so you shall plunder the Egyptians."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);












"I will sing to the LORD, for he has triumphed gloriously;  
    horse and rider he has thrown into the sea.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Song of Moses'),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 2, 'The LORD is my strength and my might,  
    and he has become my salvation;  
this is my God, and I will praise him,  
    my father"s God, and I will exalt him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 3, 'The LORD is a warrior;  
    the LORD is his name.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 4, '"Pharaoh"s chariots and his army he cast into the sea;  
    his picked officers were sunk in the Red Sea.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 5, 'The floods covered them;  
    they went down into the depths like a stone.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 6, 'Your right hand, O LORD, glorious in power--  
    your right hand, O LORD, shattered the enemy.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 7, 'In the greatness of your majesty you overthrew your adversaries;  
    you sent out your fury, it consumed them like stubble.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 8, 'At the blast of your nostrils the waters piled up,  
    the floods stood up in a heap;  
    the deeps congealed in the heart of the sea.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 9, 'The enemy said, "I will pursue, I will overtake,  
    I will divide the spoil, my desire shall have its fill of them.  
    I will draw my sword, my hand shall destroy them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 10, 'You blew with your wind, the sea covered them;  
    they sank like lead in the mighty waters.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 11, '"Who is like you, O LORD, among the gods?  
    Who is like you, majestic in holiness,  
    awesome in splendor, doing wonders?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 12, 'You stretched out your right hand,  
    the earth swallowed them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 13, '"In your steadfast love you led the people whom you redeemed;  
    you guided them by your strength to your holy abode.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 14, 'The peoples heard, they trembled;  
    pangs seized the inhabitants of Philistia.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 15, 'Then the chiefs of Edom were dismayed;  
    trembling seized the leaders of Moab;  
    all the inhabitants of Canaan melted away.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 16, 'Terror and dread fell upon them;  
    by the might of your arm, they became still as a stone  
until your people, O LORD, passed by,  
    until the people whom you acquired passed by.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 17, 'You brought them in and planted them on the mountain of your own possession,  
    the place, O LORD, that you made your abode,  
    the sanctuary, O LORD, that your hands have established.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 18, 'The LORD will reign forever and ever."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 19, 'When the horses of Pharaoh with his chariots and his chariot drivers went into the sea, the LORD brought back the waters of the sea upon them; but the Israelites walked through the sea on dry ground.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 20, 'Then the prophet Miriam, Aaron"s sister, took a tambourine in her hand; and all the women went out after her with tambourines and with dancing.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Song of Miriam'),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 21, 'And Miriam sang to them:
"Sing to the LORD, for he has triumphed gloriously;  
horse and rider he has thrown into the sea."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 22, 'Then Moses ordered Israel to set out from the Red Sea, and they went into the wilderness of Shur. They went three days in the wilderness and found no water.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Bitter Water Made Sweet'),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 23, 'When they came to Marah, they could not drink the water of Marah because it was bitter. That is why it was called Marah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 24, 'And the people complained against Moses, saying, "What shall we drink?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 25, 'He cried out to the LORD; and the LORD showed him a piece of wood; he threw it into the water, and the water became sweet.
There the LORD made for them a statute and an ordinance and there he put them to the test.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 26, 'He said, "If you will listen carefully to the voice of the LORD your God, and do what is right in his sight, and give heed to his commandments and keep all his statutes, I will not bring upon you any of the diseases that I brought upon the Egyptians; for I am the LORD who heals you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 15, 27, 'Then they came to Elim, where there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees; and they camped there by the water.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);




When Moses had told the words of the people to the LORD,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The People Consecrated'),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 10, 'the LORD said to Moses: "Go to the people and consecrate them today and tomorrow. Have them wash their clothes', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 11, 'and prepare for the third day, because on the third day the LORD will come down upon Mount Sinai in the sight of all the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 12, 'You shall set limits for the people all around, saying, "Be careful not to go up the mountain or to touch the edge of it. Any who touch the mountain shall be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 13, 'No hand shall touch them, but they shall be stoned or shot with arrows; whether animal or human being, they shall not live." When the trumpet sounds a long blast, they may go up on the mountain."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 14, 'So Moses went down from the mountain to the people. He consecrated the people, and they washed their clothes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 15, 'And he said to the people, "Prepare for the third day; do not go near a woman."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 16, 'On the morning of the third day there was thunder and lightning, as well as a thick cloud on the mountain, and a blast of a trumpet so loud that all the people who were in the camp trembled.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 17, 'Moses brought the people out of the camp to meet God. They took their stand at the foot of the mountain.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 18, 'Now Mount Sinai was wrapped in smoke, because the LORD had descended upon it in fire; the smoke went up like the smoke of a kiln, while the whole mountain shook violently.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 19, 'As the blast of the trumpet grew louder and louder, Moses would speak and God would answer him in thunder.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 20, 'When the LORD descended upon Mount Sinai, to the top of the mountain, the LORD summoned Moses to the top of the mountain, and Moses went up.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 21, 'Then the LORD said to Moses, "Go down and warn the people not to break through to the LORD to look; otherwise many of them will perish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 22, 'Even the priests who approach the LORD must consecrate themselves or the LORD will break out against them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 23, 'Moses said to the LORD, "The people are not permitted to come up to Mount Sinai; for you yourself warned us, saying, "Set limits around the mountain and keep it holy.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 24, 'The LORD said to him, "Go down, and come up bringing Aaron with you; but do not let either the priests or the people break through to come up to the LORD; otherwise he will break out against them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 19, 25, 'So Moses went down to the people and told them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



The firstborn of your sons you shall give to me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 22, 30, 'You shall do the same with your oxen and with your sheep: seven days it shall remain with its mother; on the eighth day you shall give it to me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 22, 31, 'You shall be people consecrated to me; therefore you shall not eat any meat that is mangled by beasts in the field; you shall throw it to the dogs.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

No one shall appear before me empty-handed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 16, 'You shall observe the festival of harvest, of the first fruits of your labor, of what you sow in the field. You shall observe the festival of ingathering at the end of the year, when you gather in from the field the fruit of your labor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 17, 'Three times in the year all your males shall appear before the Lord God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 18, 'You shall not offer the blood of my sacrifice with anything leavened, or let the fat of my festival remain until the morning.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 19, 'The choicest of the first fruits of your ground you shall bring into the house of the LORD your God.
You shall not boil a kid in its mother"s milk.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 20, 'I am going to send an angel in front of you, to guard you on the way and to bring you to the place that I have prepared.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Conquest of Canaan Promised'),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 21, 'Be attentive to him and listen to his voice; do not rebel against him, for he will not pardon your transgression; for my name is in him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 22, 'But if you listen attentively to his voice and do all that I say, then I will be an enemy to your enemies and a foe to your foes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 23, 'When my angel goes in front of you, and brings you to the Amorites, the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Canaanites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites, and I blot them out,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 24, 'you shall not bow down to their gods, or worship them, or follow their practices, but you shall utterly demolish them and break their pillars in pieces.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 25, 'You shall worship the LORD your God, and I will bless your bread and your water; and I will take sickness away from among you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 26, 'No one shall miscarry or be barren in your land; I will fulfill the number of your days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 27, 'I will send my terror in front of you, and will throw into confusion all the people against whom you shall come, and I will make all your enemies turn their backs to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 28, 'And I will send the pestilence in front of you, which shall drive out the Hivites, the Canaanites, and the Hittites from before you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 29, 'I will not drive them out from before you in one year, or the land would become desolate and the wild animals would multiply against you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 30, 'Little by little I will drive them out from before you, until you have increased and possess the land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 31, 'I will set your borders from the Red Sea to the sea of the Philistines, and from the wilderness to the Euphrates; for I will hand over to you the inhabitants of the land, and you shall drive them out before you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 32, 'You shall make no covenant with them and their gods.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 23, 33, 'They shall not live in your land, or they will make you sin against me; for if you worship their gods, it will surely be a snare to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);









"It is not the sound made by victors,  
or the sound made by losers;  
it is the sound of revelers that I hear."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 19, 'As soon as he came near the camp and saw the calf and the dancing, Moses" anger burned hot, and he threw the tablets from his hands and broke them at the foot of the mountain.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 20, 'He took the calf that they had made, burned it with fire, ground it to powder, scattered it on the water, and made the Israelites drink it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 21, 'Moses said to Aaron, "What did this people do to you that you have brought so great a sin upon them?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 22, 'And Aaron said, "Do not let the anger of my lord burn hot; you know the people, that they are bent on evil.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 23, 'They said to me, "Make us gods, who shall go before us; as for this Moses, the man who brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we do not know what has become of him."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 24, 'So I said to them, "Whoever has gold, take it off"; so they gave it to me, and I threw it into the fire, and out came this calf!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 25, 'When Moses saw that the people were running wild (for Aaron had let them run wild, to the derision of their enemies),', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 26, 'then Moses stood in the gate of the camp, and said, "Who is on the LORD"s side? Come to me!" And all the sons of Levi gathered around him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 27, 'He said to them, "Thus says the LORD, the God of Israel, "Put your sword on your side, each of you! Go back and forth from gate to gate throughout the camp, and each of you kill your brother, your friend, and your neighbor.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 28, 'The sons of Levi did as Moses commanded, and about three thousand of the people fell on that day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 29, 'Moses said, "Today you have ordained yourselves for the service of the LORD, each one at the cost of a son or a brother, and so have brought a blessing on yourselves this day."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 30, 'On the next day Moses said to the people, "You have sinned a great sin. But now I will go up to the LORD; perhaps I can make atonement for your sin."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 31, 'So Moses returned to the LORD and said, "Alas, this people has sinned a great sin; they have made for themselves gods of gold.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 32, 'But now, if you will only forgive their sin--but if not, blot me out of the book that you have written."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 33, 'But the LORD said to Moses, "Whoever has sinned against me I will blot out of my book.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 34, 'But now go, lead the people to the place about which I have spoken to you; see, my angel shall go in front of you. Nevertheless, when the day comes for punishment, I will punish them for their sin."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 32, 35, 'Then the LORD sent a plague on the people, because they made the calf--the one that Aaron made.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


"The LORD, the LORD,  
a God merciful and gracious,  
slow to anger,  
and abounding in steadfast love and faithfulness,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 7, 'keeping steadfast love for the thousandth generation,  
forgiving iniquity and transgression and sin,  
yet by no means clearing the guilty,  
but visiting the iniquity of the parents  
upon the children  
and the children"s children,  
to the third and the fourth generation."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 8, 'And Moses quickly bowed his head toward the earth, and worshiped.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 9, 'He said, "If now I have found favor in your sight, O Lord, I pray, let the Lord go with us. Although this is a stiff-necked people, pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us for your inheritance."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 10, 'He said: I hereby make a covenant. Before all your people I will perform marvels, such as have not been performed in all the earth or in any nation; and all the people among whom you live shall see the work of the LORD; for it is an awesome thing that I will do with you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Covenant Renewed'),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 11, 'Observe what I command you today. See, I will drive out before you the Amorites, the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 12, 'Take care not to make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land to which you are going, or it will become a snare among you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 13, 'You shall tear down their altars, break their pillars, and cut down their sacred poles', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 14, '(for you shall worship no other god, because the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God).', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 15, 'You shall not make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, for when they prostitute themselves to their gods and sacrifice to their gods, someone among them will invite you, and you will eat of the sacrifice.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 16, 'And you will take wives from among their daughters for your sons, and their daughters who prostitute themselves to their gods will make your sons also prostitute themselves to their gods.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 17, 'You shall not make cast idols.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 18, 'You shall keep the festival of unleavened bread. Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread, as I commanded you, at the time appointed in the month of Abib; for in the month of Abib you came out from Egypt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 19, 'All that first opens the womb is mine, all your male livestock, the firstborn of cow and sheep.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 20, 'The firstborn of a donkey you shall redeem with a lamb, or if you will not redeem it you shall break its neck. All the firstborn of your sons you shall redeem.
No one shall appear before me empty-handed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 21, 'Six days you shall work, but on the seventh day you shall rest; even in plowing time and in harvest time you shall rest.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 22, 'You shall observe the festival of weeks, the first fruits of wheat harvest, and the festival of ingathering at the turn of the year.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 23, 'Three times in the year all your males shall appear before the LORD God, the God of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 24, 'For I will cast out nations before you, and enlarge your borders; no one shall covet your land when you go up to appear before the LORD your God three times in the year.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 25, 'You shall not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leaven, and the sacrifice of the festival of the passover shall not be left until the morning.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 26, 'The best of the first fruits of your ground you shall bring to the house of the LORD your God.
You shall not boil a kid in its mother"s milk.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 27, 'The LORD said to Moses: Write these words; in accordance with these words I have made a covenant with you and with Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 28, 'He was there with the LORD forty days and forty nights; he neither ate bread nor drank water. And he wrote on the tablets the words of the covenant, the ten commandments.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 29, 'Moses came down from Mount Sinai. As he came down from the mountain with the two tablets of the covenant in his hand, Moses did not know that the skin of his face shone because he had been talking with God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Shining Face of Moses'),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 30, 'When Aaron and all the Israelites saw Moses, the skin of his face was shining, and they were afraid to come near him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 31, 'But Moses called to them; and Aaron and all the leaders of the congregation returned to him, and Moses spoke with them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 32, 'Afterward all the Israelites came near, and he gave them in commandment all that the LORD had spoken with him on Mount Sinai.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 33, 'When Moses had finished speaking with them, he put a veil on his face;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 34, 'but whenever Moses went in before the LORD to speak with him, he would take the veil off, until he came out; and when he came out, and told the Israelites what he had been commanded,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(2, 'Kel', 'Exodus', 34, 35, 'the Israelites would see the face of Moses, that the skin of his face was shining; and Moses would put the veil on his face again, until he went in to speak with him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);







